Que. What is meant by returns to a factor? State the law of diminishing returns to a
factor.
Ans. Returns to a Factor It refers to the behaviour of output when only one
variable factor of production is increased in short-run and fixed factors
remain constant.
Law of Diminishing Returns to a Factor
It refers to a situation in which total output increases at a diminishing rate
when more and more variable factor is combined with the fixed factor of
production. In this situation, marginal product of the variable factor must be
diminishing.
