Que. Why MP curve cuts AP curve at its maximum point?
Next
Toppers
Ans. It happens because when AP rises, MP is more than AP. When AP falls, MP
is less than AP. So, it is only when AP is constant and at its maximum point,
that MP is equal to AP. Therefore, MP curve cuts AP curve at its maximum
point..
